# Local-only operator secrets and local coverage snapshots.
# W1 secret-leak remediation (PR4a follow-up). Narrow scope: project root
# only; no recursive or double-star patterns. The ``.codegraph`` index and
# ``.env.example`` template (if added) remain tracked.
/.env
/coverage.json
/coverage_full.json

# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tailwind v4 build artifacts
tailwindcss/node_modules/
tailwindcss/package-lock.json

# Tool config with secrets in plaintext (InsForge API key)
# DO NOT commit. Use environment variables instead.
opencode.json

# External artifacts accidentally placed in the project root by other systems.
# Not project source — keep them local.
.openclaw/
SOUL.md
.audit-venv/

# Per-gate indicator envelopes (deterministic-quality-harness v1.5 Rule 16).
# Generated by `python scripts/check_*.py --emit-envelope quality/<gate>.json`
# and aggregated by `python scripts/quality_report.py quality` (CI step
# summary). The directory is empty until the first CI run after this entry;
# keeping it out of git keeps the repo free of build artifacts.
#
# The leading `/` anchors the pattern to the repo root. Without it, git
# also matches a `quality/` directory at any depth, which would silently
# exclude the tracked `docs/quality/` tree introduced for issue #434.
# Tracked files are not actually ignored by git, but `git add` and other
# plumbing treat them as ignored and demand `-f`, which is exactly the
# regression this entry caused.
# quality/  # removed in favor of the anchored rule below
/quality/
# Gentle AI review artifact JSONs (produced by `gentle-ai review` runs).
# These are written to repo root by older runs and pollute `git status`.
# Pattern is broad (.gentle-ai*.json) so any future prefix is also ignored.
.gentle-ai*.json

# Pi editor runtime state (analogous to .codegraph-vba/, .engram/).
.pi/

# Local Pi runtime state
# Directory-first order is REQUIRED: .atl/ establishes the directory, !.atl/
# un-ignores it for traversal, .atl/*.md re-ignores .md files, and
# !.atl/skill-registry.md keeps the tracked registry file un-ignored.
.atl/
!.atl/
.atl/*.md
!.atl/skill-registry.md
